The evaporation of one mole of water has a standard Gibbs free energy change, $\Delta G^{\ominus}$, of $+8.6\text{ kJ}$ at $25^{\circ}\text{C}$.

Sketch a graph on the axes to show how $\Delta G^{\ominus}$ changes for this process between $25^{\circ}\text{C}$ and $150^{\circ}\text{C}$ at $101\text{ kPa}$.

